format session-log-v1
stamp 20260820.143646
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan ladder fold -- the word came, 523 checks moved home, and the meter became a wall
prompt Taking inspiration from our outer and inner recursion loops, approve all recommendations like your fold recommendation.
think Read the ask as the word the parked recommendation was waiting for. The outer loop is the arc, one rung a lap, each log recommending the next; the inner loop is the ladder each rung carries. Approving every standing recommendation means the ungated ones keep going and the one gated door -- the ladder-copy fold, parked at Keaton's word since 20260820.132327 -- finally opens.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md reads CLOSED or Released, so no red preempts constructive work and the fold may open honestly.
think Read the design call whole before touching anything. Option A: make the checks pub and call them. Its correctness rests on the measurement -- bodies byte-identical today cannot disagree tomorrow -- so the fold is mechanical wherever they match, and that is exactly the claim to test rather than trust.
think Confirmed the shape by reading rather than recalling: a rung's implementation forwards to the rung below (regards, heeded_in, regard_holds in recount all return reweighing_rung's), so a carried check exercises the same code either way. That is what makes calling it below equivalent at all.
think First cut folded every byte-identical body whose whole call subtree was also carried. It compiled, the top rung ran GREEN, and the ladder read copies=0. Then the choir named apprise RED.
think The cause was worth more than the lines it cost. Each rung keeps its notes in its own directory, so a folded wire check provisions the rung below's wire and leaves this rung's cold -- NoteUnavailable, a debt that could not be seated at all. It passed on a warm tree and failed the moment caravan_suite cleared the stores. REDS %92's cold-start discipline caught a fault I had already proven GREEN by hand.
think The second limit surfaced in the same cut: a check whose tail chains into a check this rung invented cannot run below, because the rung below has never heard of the check it would chain to. The chain simply ends early, silently, with no compiler complaint -- which is how the first cut lost check_apprise_wire.
think So the fold narrowed to a rule I can state: a check runs in the rung below only when it takes no wire (empty parameter list) and everything it transitively calls folds too. 523 of 779 carried bodies qualify. The rest are named rather than rounded away, and they are precisely what option B takes.
obs Parity was the proof, not the compile. Every rung of the grievance arc from appraise to recount was built twice -- folded and pristine, from a git worktree at HEAD -- and run against the same wire: 28 rungs, the same output lines, every one of them. Only three concurrent dependents interleave their prints, in the pristine build exactly as in the folded one.
obs The meter changed jobs with the fold. It began as a ratchet over a number nobody watched; it is now the wall that keeps the fold folded -- ceiling 22,000 against a standing of 12,035, about six rungs of headroom at the residue's own measured rate, where the old 60,000 over a folded ladder would have meant nothing for years. It also counts the 523 folded checks off the ladder itself, so a tree that quietly carried the bodies again goes RED whatever the prose says.
obs The design call's own numbers were 88 modules and 46,014 carried lines; the ladder has grown two rungs since. Both readings are kept rather than reconciled away -- 46,014 is what the call measured, 54,612 is what the fold actually moved against.
obs The bolder cut is not lost work. It measured the ceiling of what a pure body-identity fold can reach (46,061 lines) and taught the two limits by failing on metal, which is why the addendum names them as limits rather than as shortfalls.
loom witness=caravan_ladder_copy modules=90 checks=1070 distinct=814 copies=256 copied_lines=12035 ceiling=22000 folded_checks=523
loom fold=caravan_ladder before_copies=779 before_copied_lines=54612 lines_removed=39962 ladder_before=289303 ladder_after=249341 top_rung_before=15664 top_rung_after=13113
loom fold=caravan_ladder marginal_before=4383 marginal_after=1637 parity_rungs=28 parity_same=28
loom witness=caravan_suite rungs=85 verdict=green cold_start=true
file caravan/*.rye 88 rung modules folded -- every check pub, 523 of them run in the rung that owns them
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_copy_scan.sh reads pub checks, ceiling now 22000, and says plainly what stays carried and why
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish four claims now -- the standing, the fold counted off the ladder, the counting by hand, and three refusals by name
file active-designing/20260820-131713_caravan-ladder-shared-harness.md Status Landed, with an addendum naming what moved, what did not, and why
file caravan/README.md the durable module-side record of the fold, its two limits, and the parity that proves nothing changed
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back to the whole pre-fold ladder, since b8427b4d1b is where a rung reads as its author left it
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge moves from the recount rung to the fold; the prior edge condenses to a pointer
recommend keep-going the inner loop is answered as far as body identity can answer it: 523 checks live in one place now, the ladder is 39,962 lines lighter, and the meter that measured the ratchet has become the wall that keeps it. What stands above is option B, and the fold just made it a refactor rather than a rewrite -- a harness that runs a rung's checks against its own report and its own wire, with the chain written as a list rather than a tail call, has neither limit that stopped this cut, and it would take the remaining 12,035 lines. Beside it the outer loop stands exactly where it was: nothing yet reads whether a second look finally settles the matter, exactly as nothing read a reader's verdict until the suffice rung.
